# FABLE-OPUS-GATE-CLEANUP-20260926-197 (b): a send whose text field is not empty copies its bytes
# (l2_emit_send: memcpy), so the generated program includes <string.h> -- the preamble names it only
# where the program's own emission uses it.  The host root writes the exit letter's stderr text,
# "hi": on stderr, so it does not run into the driver's stdout line (a text literal has no newline).
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "hi")
return
